  "body": "Converting the options argument of getContext() can run script. Previously that happened after the context mode had been consulted, so script could call getContext() again (or transfer the canvas) and end up with two rendering contexts for a single canvas. Now options are converted first and the context mode is consulted afterwards.\n\nAlso modernize the prose of the affected algorithms.\n\n---\n\nThe WebGL specification needs to accept the converted `WebGLContextAttributes` dictionary: KhronosGroup/WebGL#3807.\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * WebKit: matches as of https://commits.webkit.org/316107@main\n   * Chromium appears to match already, as it converts the options dictionary before `getContext()` runs (#3395), but this needs confirming.\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/65525\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: …\n   * Gecko: …\n   * WebKit: fixed in https://commits.webkit.org/316107@main\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13305/canvas.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 5:09 PM UTC (15c9808)\">/canvas.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13305/0e292f4...15c9808/canvas.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 5:09 PM UTC (15c9808)\">diff</a> )",
